{"archetypes":[{"name":"call-site-coverage","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Checks that the three launcher call sites named in the plan are exhaustive — missing default-mode callers would re-introduce the same latent defect the plan purports to fix.","prompt_body":"Enumerate every invocation of `run-external-agent.sh` (or its `$RUN_EXTERNAL_AGENT_SH`-override equivalent) across the entire repo, then compare that set against the three sites the plan names (`launch-codex-implement.sh`, `lint-fix-loop.sh`, `review-and-fix.sh`). For each invocation not in the plan's list, determine whether it is a default-mode lane with a custom stderr sink; if so, flag it as a coverage gap the plan must address. Verify that the capture-mode and Cursor lanes the plan intentionally exempts are truly exercising the capture path and not a custom fd2 redirect that would make them subject to the same defect. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sink-var-timing","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Checks that in each launcher the sink variable forwarded via --stderr-sink is guaranteed non-empty at the call site — an unset or late-initialized variable silently passes an empty string and degrades to the broken fallback order the plan is fixing.","prompt_body":"For each of the three launchers the plan modifies, trace the initialization of the sink variable (`$SIDECAR_LOG` in `launch-codex-implement.sh`; `$codex_wrapper_log` in `lint-fix-loop.sh` and `review-and-fix.sh`) from its definition to the `run-external-agent.sh` call site where `--stderr-sink` will be added. Confirm the variable is unconditionally set to a non-empty path by the time the wrapper is invoked on every execution path, and flag any code path where it could be empty, unset, or defined after the call site. Also check whether the `validate_meta_scalar_path` guard the plan adds in `run-external-agent.sh` rejects an empty string, or whether an empty `--stderr-sink` value would silently pass validation and leave the fix inoperative. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
